; foldnine.dev - mail records for Migadu.
;
; Import into Cloudflare: DNS > Records > Import and Export > Import.
; Leave "Proxy imported DNS records" UNCHECKED. Proxying a DKIM CNAME makes
; Cloudflare answer with its own address instead of the key, DKIM then fails
; and the mail lands in spam.
;
; Cloudflare ignores SOA and apex NS on import, so neither is here.
;
; The first seven records were imported on 2026-09-18 and are live. Cloudflare's
; import ADDS records rather than replacing them, so do not re-import this file
; over a zone that already has them - a second SPF record is as invalid as none.
; This file is the intended state of the zone, for a rebuild or a move.

$ORIGIN foldnine.dev.
$TTL 3600

; --- where mail for the domain is delivered --------------------------------
@	3600	IN	MX	10 aspmx1.migadu.com.
@	3600	IN	MX	20 aspmx2.migadu.com.

; --- who is allowed to send as this domain ---------------------------------
; Exactly one SPF record. Two are as invalid as none.
@	3600	IN	TXT	"v=spf1 include:spf.migadu.com -all"

; --- proof the domain is yours ---------------------------------------------
; Issued per domain by Migadu, under Domains once foldnine.dev is added. It is
; published in DNS for anyone to read, so it is not a secret.
@	3600	IN	TXT	"hosted-email-verify=d7sk0efg"

; --- DKIM signing keys ------------------------------------------------------
; The target is fully qualified and contains the domain twice on purpose.
key1._domainkey	3600	IN	CNAME	key1.foldnine.dev._domainkey.migadu.com.
key2._domainkey	3600	IN	CNAME	key2.foldnine.dev._domainkey.migadu.com.
key3._domainkey	3600	IN	CNAME	key3.foldnine.dev._domainkey.migadu.com.

; --- what receivers should do with mail that fails the checks ---------------
; p=none reports without rejecting. Move to quarantine after a month of clean
; reports, once the aggregate reports show nothing legitimate is failing.
_dmarc	3600	IN	TXT	"v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:uros@foldnine.dev"
